===== RERUN 1 =====
# device NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 Laptop GPU SMs=82 cc=12.0 (clocks LOCKED 1860 via nvidia-smi -lgc)
# UNIT = one 32-K-value tile step. k16 arm = 2 MMA + 2-term fold; k32 arm = 1 MMA + 1-term fold.
# SASS contract (verify with cuobjdump -sass): IMMA count per instantiation = NACC*2*unroll (k16), NACC*1*unroll (k32).

## NACC CONTROL -- 1 CTA of 4 warps, clock64 cyc per 32-K tile step
# arm                           NACC=1    NACC=2    NACC=4    NACC=8   NACC=16
  K16 (2 MMA + 2-fold)         61.5039   68.5027   67.2513   60.5013   60.3757
  K32 (1 MMA + 1-fold)         26.5039   30.3772   50.1265   51.0012   23.9388
  -> tile-step ratio NACC=1  : 2.3206x
  -> tile-step ratio NACC=2  : 2.2551x
  -> tile-step ratio NACC=4  : 1.3416x
  -> tile-step ratio NACC=8  : 1.1863x
  -> tile-step ratio NACC=16 : 2.5221x
  (instruction-only bound, from rate_audit.cu 12-form table, is 1.997x)

## FULL-GPU wall clock (grid=82 CTAs x 256 thr; NACC=8, best of 5)
  K16 (2 MMA + 2-fold)           0.712 ms
  K32 (1 MMA + 1-fold)           0.502 ms
  -> full-GPU tile-step speedup of the k32 form: 1.4199x
